melody:
# Chorus (the original is in cut time; written here with quarter-note beats)
Ev-'ry morn-ing, ev-'ry eve-ning, ain't we got fun?
Bb3 G4 F#4 G4 Bb3 G4 F#4 G4 r Ab4 Ab4 G4 Ab4(4)
Not much mon-ey, oh, but hon-ey, ain't we got fun?
Bb3 Ab4 G4 Ab4 Bb3 Ab4 G4 Ab4 r Bb4 Bb4 A4 Bb4(4)
The rent's un-paid, dear, we have-n't a bus,
r C5 B4 C5 Eb5 r Eb4(2) ~Eb4 Eb4 Eb4/ F4/ G4 Bb4(4)
but smiles were made, dear, for peo-ple like us.
r Bb4 A4 G4 D5 r D4(2) ~D4 C5 C5/ Bb4/ A4 G4 r r(2)
In the win-ter, in the sum-mer, don't we have fun?
Bb3 G4 F#4 G4 Bb3 G4 F#4 G4 r Ab4 Ab4 G4 Ab4(4)
Times are bum and get-ting bum-mer, still we have fun.
Bb3 Ab4 G4 Ab4 Bb3 Ab4 G4 Ab4 r Bb4 Bb4 A4 Bb4(4)
There's noth-ing sur-er: the rich get rich and the poor get chil-dren.
r C5 B4 C5 D5(2) Eb5. E5/ F5 Eb5 D5 C5/ C5/ Bb4 Eb5 Eb4 F4
In the mean-time, in be-tween time, ain't we got fun?
r G4/ G4/ F#4 G4 r G4/ G4/ F#4 G4 r Bb4 A4 G4 Eb4 r r(2)

# Second chorus
Ev-'ry morn-ing, ev-'ry eve-ning, don't we have fun?
Bb3 G4 F#4 G4 Bb3 G4 F#4 G4 r Ab4 Ab4 G4 Ab4(4)
Twins and cares, dear, come in pairs, dear, don't we have fun?
Bb3 Ab4 G4 Ab4 Bb3 Ab4 G4 Ab4 r Bb4 Bb4 A4 Bb4(4)
We've on-ly start-ed as mom-mer and pop,
r C5 B4 C5 Eb5 r Eb4(2) ~Eb4 Eb4 Eb4/ F4/ G4 Bb4(4)
are we down-heart-ed? I'll say that we're not!
r Bb4 A4 G4 D5 r D4(2) ~D4 C5 C5/ Bb4/ A4 G4 r r(2)
Land-lords mad and get-ting mad-der, ain't we got fun?
Bb3 G4 F#4 G4 Bb3 G4 F#4 G4 r Ab4 Ab4 G4 Ab4(4)
Times are bad and get-ting bad-der, still we have fun.
Bb3 Ab4 G4 Ab4 Bb3 Ab4 G4 Ab4 r Bb4 Bb4 A4 Bb4(4)
There's noth-ing sur-er: the rich get rich and the poor get laid off.
r C5 B4 C5 D5(2) Eb5. E5/ F5 Eb5 D5 C5/ C5/ Bb4 Eb5 Eb4 F4
In the mean-time, in be-tween time, ain't we got fun?
r G4/ G4/ F#4 G4 r G4/ G4/ F#4 G4 r Bb4 A4 G4 Eb4(4)
